# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on the way out of
# git. That silently changes bytes this repository asserts on: `tests/test_packaging.py` pins the
# SHA-256 of LICENSE against the verbatim GPLv3 text from gnu.org, and it failed on a
# windows-latest runner for exactly this reason. Normalising to LF in the working tree keeps a
# checkout byte-identical on every platform, which is also what the packaging tests compare and
# what `atomic_write` produces (it pins newline="\n" for the same reason).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Documents whose bytes are asserted or shipped verbatim: never touch their line endings at all.
LICENSE -text
eve_skills/data/*.json -text
